      "calculationScope": "EXACT_MANUAL_CALCULATION",
      "manualArithmetic": "No assigned numerical exercise: all source equations and force directions checked. Reviewer probes only: (10-6)N/4kg=1m/s²; N=mg+may-Fup gives 2(10+3)=26N, rather than 20N. Zero resultant integrates to arbitrary constant v0, which may be nonzero. Third-law forces cancel in the combined system; an isolated body receives only its own interaction member.",
      "manualFeasibility": "PASS_AI_EXACT",
      "physicalAssumptions": "Classical inertial frame and constant positive mass. Isolate the chosen body and distinguish received forces from forces it exerts. The perpendicular contact normal must satisfy N>=0; N=mg additionally needs zero normal acceleration and no other normal component. Zero net force does not imply zero velocity. For extended static bodies, the source explicitly also requires moment balance.",
      "pedagogicalReview": "Identifies agents and a one-body force diagram before signed components and equations. Explicitly avoids assuming N=mg or cancelling a third-law pair on one body. Notes that extended equilibrium also needs moment balance. No choice options or hidden numerical calculator step.",
