      "manualArithmetic": "The source teaches symbolic relations, with no assigned numerical exercise. Reviewer probes: 4N over 3m at angles 0, pi/2, pi give 12,0,-12J. The spring-force integral gives -kx²/2. Newton F=m*dv/dt dotted with v equals d(mv²/2)/dt. For m=2kg, vi=1m/s, work=12J: Ki=1J, Kf=13J, vf=sqrt(13)m/s exactly; no decimal is required. Uniform motion with motor +10N and resistance -10N at 2m/s for 3s gives individual works ±60J and net zero. W=beta*t² yields instantaneous power 2beta*t and average power beta*t.",
